thermus.body:
Admins could save an HTTPS OTLP receiver, but could not route events directly to an Axiom dataset. This change adds one optional dataset field to the existing Audit destination. Save, saved Test and queued export use the same revision; a blank dataset keeps generic OTLP behavior. System logging is unchanged.

The hosted app also selects the complete approved organization Audit notice bundle. Matching website text is in [Marketing #27](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus-Marketing/pull/27). Settings backup and recovery move to Slice 4, as requested.

## Review

**T2 Need architect.** Architecture: T2: declarations changed in 2 public modules; 5 registry views edited.
SQL migration and changed legal disclosures also require review. Overall merge status: **merged** as [`a7411fd0`](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/commit/a7411fd02aa6dd3300b334d4585f71469071b499). The owner approved this head as architect and approved the exact notice package and internal-organization disposition. [Human approval](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/a7284b0c4dc02a8c7cd7958cfdc4a11ce4adee89/ast-report/s2-04-rollout/approvals/owner-approval.json).

