- Before: generic endpoint and optional Bearer token. After: the same atomic settings revision can include an Axiom dataset. Stale queued work is dropped; already-authorized sends may finish.
- The existing sender adds one fixed routing header after validation. Dataset and credentials remain outside Audit event payloads.
- App composition selects new legal versions and hashes. Previous accepted bundles remain immutable; existing organization agreements are not rewritten.
- The additive database column permits old code to run, but old code cannot route Axiom events. Disable export before rolling back to that code; retain schema and encryption key.

The deployed connection verifies TLS to the Supabase session pooler. PostgreSQL reported SSL off for the pooler’s database session; end-to-end TLS is not established.

Delivery remains best effort, with bounded content, possible loss/duplicates, no history/replay, and no settings backup in this slice. Approved public notices and the Render deployment are live. The disabled destination survived a service restart with its revision and encrypted token intact. The deployed Test/Enable/MCP/Admin receipt checks await Mac unlock; export and auto-deploy remain off. [Rollout status](https://github.com/tomer-mayara/Thermus/blob/a99440ea6cf302abc04e0de11e630dcd12d37427/ast-report/s2-04-rollout/postmerge/progress-before-unlock.json).

